# Phase 2b GREEN — profitable-article-writer Sprint 1
# 9/9 PROP oracle tests PASS with real orchestration logic (no fake-to-pass).
#
# NOTE ON THE ONE TEST-MECHANICS FIX (transparent):
# The builder's Green pass reached 8/9; the 9th (test-prop1-no-model-literal.sh) failed on a genuine
# TEST-AUTHORING bug, NOT an implementation defect:
#   line 24 was:  dhits="$(grep -Ec "$FORBIDDEN" "$draft" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)"
# `grep -Ec` exits 1 when it finds ZERO matches, so on a correctly literal-free draft the `|| echo 0`
# fallback ALSO fires -> stdout becomes "0\n0" -> dhits != "0" -> the assertion could never pass even on a
# clean draft. Reproduced independently by the main agent.
#
# FIX (main agent, builder role): line 24 ->
#   dhits="$(grep -Ec "$FORBIDDEN" "$draft" 2>/dev/null)"; dhits="${dhits:-0}"
#
# ADVERSARIAL PROOF the fixed test is NOT vacuous (still catches a real violation):
#   clean draft ("no literals")         -> dhits=[0] -> assertion PASS   (correct)
#   dirty draft ("...claude-3-opus...")  -> dhits=[1] -> assertion FAILS  (catches the literal — correct)
# Only the broken grep idiom was corrected; the PROP-1 obligation is intact.
#
# Independent re-run by the main agent (maker != checker):

