# =====================================================================================================
# Sprint-1 IMPLEMENTATION-REVIEW FIX ROUND (Phase 3, FIND-001..004, builder role) — real fixes, no
# fake-to-pass. Adversary confirmed the core logic (fail-closed publish, 3-round ceiling, Mode A never
# publishes, v05 (a)-(d) genuinely model-judged with no draft regex, no model literal) is CORRECT; the
# gaps below are test-coverage + tier-labeling + 2 small bugs.
# =====================================================================================================
#
# FIND-001 (major, edge_case_coverage): EVERY test reaching gates/v0.sh or gates/v05.sh did so exclusively
# via ARTICLE_TEST_FORCE_V0/ARTICLE_TEST_FORCE_V05, so the real (non-forced) heading/size/line-count check
# in v0.sh, the real judge_v05 response-file parser in v05.sh, and the real criterion-(e) sentence-length
# arithmetic in v05.sh had ZERO test coverage. FIX: added tests/test-v0-real.sh (invokes gates/v0.sh with
# ARTICLE_TEST_FORCE_V0 unset: a well-formed draft (heading + adequate size/lines) real-PASSes; a malformed
# draft (no heading, too short) real-FAILs; a missing draft artifact real-FAILs) and tests/test-v05-real.sh
# (invokes gates/v05.sh with ARTICLE_TEST_FORCE_V05 unset: a short-sentence draft computes crit_e=true via
# the real arithmetic; a long-sentence draft (2/3 sentences >60 chars) computes crit_e=false; a real
# ARTICLE_JUDGE_V05_RESPONSE file with V05_CRIT_a..d: true lines is parsed correctly by the real parser,
# producing an overall PASS; an absent/missing response file fails closed to (a)-(d)=false and
# V05_RESULT=FAIL even though (e) alone would be true — proving the fail-closed-when-unwired claim is
# actually exercised, not just asserted in a comment). Both picked up automatically by tests/run-red.sh's
# test-*.sh glob (12 files now). SKILL.md's Status section corrected: removed the inaccurate "tests pass
# green against that real logic" claim and added an explicit "wiring vs real-gate mechanics" section
# naming which test files cover which.
#
# FIND-002 (major, verification_readiness): specs/verification-architecture.md labeled PROP-5/PROP-6 as
# Tier T2 "integration/property (no-mock)", but their tests (test-prop5-failclosed-publish.sh,
# test-prop6-modeA-draft.sh) drive the gates exclusively via the ARTICLE_TEST_FORCE_V0/V05 injection seam —
# a mock, not a no-mock integration test. FIX: relabeled PROP-5/PROP-6 in verification-architecture.md to
# state honestly that they prove fail-closed WIRING via a documented, deterministic injected-seam (T1), and
# that the REAL gate mechanics are now covered no-mock (T2) by test-v0-real.sh/test-v05-real.sh.
# contracts/sprint-1.md's CRIT-001/CRIT-002/CRIT-007 passThresholds + body sections updated to reference the
# new real-gate tests. No claim of "no-mock" remains where injection is actually used.
#
# FIND-003 (minor, implementation_correctness): run.sh:167-168 and run.sh:197-198 interpolated the raw
# $topic value unescaped into hand-built JSON for state/failures.jsonl — a doublequote or embedded newline
# in an agent-picked topic would corrupt the JSONL ledger (invalid JSON or a broken one-object-per-line
# contract). FIX: added a json_escape() helper to run.sh (uses python3 json.dumps when available, a sed
# fallback otherwise) and applied it to $topic at both failure-record call sites. Added an assertion to
# tests/test-prop15-3round-abort.sh: a topic containing a doublequote + an embedded newline still yields
# EXACTLY one physical line in failures.jsonl, and (when python3 is available) that line parses as valid
# JSON via json.loads with the topic value round-tripping correctly.
#
# FIND-004 (minor, structural_integrity): identity/accounts.sh:44-56's PROVEN_SELF_CREATE_RAILS case
# statement was dead — both arms produced "unavailable" because PROVEN_SELF_CREATE_RAILS was an
# unconditional empty-string literal, so the matched arm could never be reached even by a test. FIX: (1)
# PROVEN_SELF_CREATE_RAILS is now a CONDITIONAL default (`: "${PROVEN_SELF_CREATE_RAILS:=}"`, same pattern
# as lib/config.sh's RECORD_EARN_USES_LLM), still empty by default for Sprint 1 (honest: no proven
# self-create rail exists yet) but now externally injectable; (2) the matched-rail arm now resolves to a
# status DISTINCT from the default arm ("self-create-eligible" vs "unavailable"), making the branch
# structurally meaningful. Added test cases to tests/test-prop12-account-absent.sh: injecting
# PROVEN_SELF_CREATE_RAILS="note" + NOTE_SELF_CREATE=1 asserts the distinct "self-create-eligible" status
# (rc=0, no crash, no error text); the same injected proven-rail list with NO self-create flag set still
# degrades to "unavailable" (proving the flag AND the proven-list membership are both required, not just
# one).
